{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdzZDKdP7WYqDi5TPPJTK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan for Order 7841 Payment Timeout\n\n1. **Call `payments.provider_status()`** immediately to check if the provider is alive and responsive (rules out a complete outage).\n\n2. **Call `payments.get(order_id=7841)`** to check whether a payment record was actually created despite the timeout.\n\n3. **Branch on the result:**\n   - **If payment exists:** Do NOT retry submit. Confirm the payment to the customer.\n   - **If no payment exists AND provider is healthy:** Wait 5–10 seconds, then call `payments.submit(order_id=7841, amount_usd=120.00)` **once more** (safe retry after cold-start). This is a typical cold-start scenario where the first call timed out in-flight.\n   - **If no payment exists AND provider is unhealthy:** Hold and escalate; do not retry yet.\n\n4. **After the retry:** Immediately call `payments.get(order_id=7841)` again to verify success before confirming to the customer.\n\n**Explicit statement:** Yes, I would call `payments.submit` again, but **only once**, only after confirming no payment was created, only if the provider is responsive, and only with a check-before-retry pattern using `get()`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":260,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":297,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
